ayRef]) -> Result<Rows, ArrowError> {\n        let num_rows = columns.first().map(|x| x.len()).unwrap_or(0);\n        let mut rows = self.empty_rows(num_rows, 0);\n        self.append(&mut rows, columns)?;\n        Ok(rows)\n    }","range":{"byteOffset":{"start":44953,"end":45222},"start":{"line":1003,"column":4},"end":{"line":1008,"column":5}},"style":"primary"},{"text":"convert_columns","range":{"byteOffset":{"start":44960,"end":44975},"start":{"line":1003,"column":11},"end":{"line":1003,"column":26}},"style":"secondary"}]},{"text":"pub fn convert_rows<'a, I>(&self, rows: I) -> Result<Vec<ArrayRef>, ArrowError>\n    where\n        I: IntoIterator<Item = Row<'a>>,\n    {\n        let mut validate_utf8 = false;\n        let mut rows: Vec<_> = rows\n            .into_iter()\n            .map(|row| {\n                assert!(\n                    Arc::ptr_eq(&row.config.fields, &self.fields),\n                    \"rows were not produced by this RowConverter\"\n                );\n                validate_utf8 |= row.config.validate_utf8;\n                row.data\n            })\n            .collect();\n\n        // SAFETY\n        // We have validated that the rows came from this [`RowConverter`]\n        // and therefore must be valid\n        let result = unsafe { self.convert_raw(&mut rows, validate_utf8) }?;\n\n        if cfg!(debug_assertions) {\n            for (i, row) in rows.iter().enumerate() {\n                if !row.is_empty() {\n                    return Err(ArrowError::InvalidArgumentError(format!(\n                        \"Codecs {codecs:?} did not consume all bytes for row {i}, remaining bytes: {row:?}\",\n                        codecs = self.codecs\n                    )));\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        Ok(result)\n    }","range":{"byteOffset":{"start":49198,"end":50417},"start":{"line":1112,"column":4},"end":{"line":1146,"column":5}},"file":"sources/arrow-row-59.3.0/src/lib.rs","lines":"    pub fn convert_rows<'a, I>(